# Without these, changing a module declaration leaves every .dis here
# stale: mkdis's own "%.dis: $MODULES $SYS_MODULE" rule is the tree's
# way of saying a .b depends on the .m files it includes, and this
# directory declared none.  Editing module/dynsys.m and rebuilding
# silently left models compiled against the old adt, which then failed
# to load with a link typecheck error against a library they had just
# been built beside.
